From f15e6f9648aa3cfc267c643a58f049fe92bb3211 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:45:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-298: OW-036 draft penalty default on, ngram-mod
 miss-cost cap, MoE-union counter

OW-036 draft recent-token penalty defaults to k=4 strength=3.0 (HQ78 Q7b: lossless, long prompts +2..+4.5%); LLAMA_SPEC_DRAFT_RECENT_PENALTY=0:0 turns it off. LLAMA_SPEC_NGRAM_CAP0=c caps each ngram-mod draft at c tokens after a miss and doubles the cap on every fully accepted draft up to n_max, so a miss costs a (c+1)-row verify instead of an (n_max+1)-row one (cold copy lost 7.5% ungated). LLAMA_MOE_UNION_LOG=1 installs a cb_eval that counts distinct experts per ubatch per layer on ffn_moe_topk (untimed use only: it splits the graph).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Lane: lane-298
(cherry picked from commit 1c4d20f0fbc98004e23211f214ff80fabd1f070e)

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - fork-authored (lane-298); no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: part of win W8, OW-036 draft recent-token penalty (pk4s3): long +2..+4.5%, other prompts flat, ids 12/12; cells/combo-10050615-*, ngcap* [release ledger Table 1 W8]
